---

Classification Justification

SO-F-004 defines the capability required to transform an interpreted operating context into an adaptive decision suitable for subsequent authorization and execution.

It is derived from the root Functional Objective SO-F-001 and operates downstream of the contextual interpretation capability established by SO-F-003.

Its responsibility is limited to decision generation and does not extend to physical execution or the automatic authorization of generated decisions.

---

Operational Role

SO-F-004 occupies the decision-generation stage of the current adaptive processing flow:

Observations
      ↓
Operating Context
      ↓
Decision Generation
      ↓
Generated Decision

---

Classification Boundaries

SO-F-004 shall remain distinct from:

- Environmental perception.
- Operating-context interpretation.
- Decision authorization.
- Physical action execution.

---

Classification Notes

- Derived from SO-F-001.
- Operationally follows SO-F-003.
- Operationally precedes the execution capability established by SO-F-005.
- Represents the decision-generation stage of the current adaptive processing architecture.
- Does not establish decision authority by itself.
- The architectural position of authorization remains under investigation.
- Future decision-generation objectives shall maintain traceability to SO-F-004.
